# caravan_heed_witness.rish -- Caravan heed witness.
#
# `endure.rye` opened the last door: a quarrel its holder still presses outlives
# the run that heard it, one byte in the only note a provisioning leaves alone.
# Every run after that one opens knowing -- and knowing is all it does.
#
#   A PLAN RUN UNDER A QUARREL IT INHERITED SAYS SO IN THE WORD AN OPERATOR
#   READS.
#
# WHAT THIS RUNG PROVES, MEASURED:
#
#   * THE NUMBER THE TWO PLANS DISAGREE ON IS PLANS REPORTED CARRIED WHILE A
#     QUARREL INHERITED FROM AN EARLIER RUN STOOD AGAINST THEM. Every rung
#     beneath this one hears, records, escorts, tells, and carries; none of them
#     asks the run receiving a position to answer for it. It falls from 1 to 0.
#   * A WORD PUBLISHED AS THOUGH NOBODY HAD OBJECTED, below this rung. The bare
#     run inherits a live quarrel, carries its work out whole, settles `carried`,
#     and leaves `caravan/.heeds/plan.regard` unwritten -- so the operator who
#     opens the outcome reads nothing at all about the position standing over it.
#   * THE WORD IS NOT SOFTENED, ONLY ACCOMPANIED. Both runs settle `carried out
#     whole`. A supervisor can neither resolve a quarrel nor withdraw one; what it
#     can do is refuse to publish its outcome as if the quarrel were not there.
#   * A REGARD IS READ BEFORE THE RECORD IS TAKEN UP. The heeding reads the
#     standing note as the first act of the run and publishes only at the end,
#     because `endure` writes that same note last -- so a plan reading it after
#     its own work would be reading its own handwriting back as somebody else's
#     judgment. This run's reader ACCEPTS, on purpose: nothing it heard itself
#     could account for the regard it publishes.
#   * A POSITION IS WEIGHED, AND NEVER WITHDRAWN. No run of this plan writes the
#     standing note and no run clears it. `plan.standing` reads `p` after the
#     weighing run, untouched by the very act of answering it.
#   * A QUARREL SURVIVES A PROVISIONING AND THE WORD ABOUT IT DOES NOT -- proven
#     as its own fold, since the seam between the two is the whole rung: a
#     quarrel belongs to the person holding it, a word about that quarrel belongs
#     to the run that said it.
#   * THE PRICE IS ONE BYTE BESIDE A SETTLEMENT THE RUN HAD ALREADY PUBLISHED.
#     Both runs take up 6 phases, absorb 3 into standing dependents, lose 3 arcs,
#     take the same judgment back, re-seat the same 3 phases, spend the same 6
#     dependents, post and carry the same correction, read the same accepting
#     answer, record the same disagreement, escort the same published word, ask
#     the same reader, stand the same mark, tell the same raiser, carry the same
#     position past themselves, and settle the plan `carried`.
#   * A PLAN PUBLISHES WHETHER IT READS UNDER THE QUARREL IT INHERITED. The word
#     is plan-level beside the endurance, since it instructs about what a run says
#     of its own whole outcome rather than about one arc.
#   * FOUR REFUSALS THIS RUNG EARNS, EACH ABOUT WHAT A RUN OWES A POSITION IT DID
#     NOT MAKE. `HeedEarly` is the moment. `HeedUnpressed` is the hard half -- a
#     word standing under a byte no endurance would ever have written publishes an
#     objection nobody ever made. `HeedMiscounted` is the honesty of the count.
#     `HeedMisrecorded` is the record -- an operator takes that byte and the
#     settlement together as the whole outcome.
#   * A PLAN NOBODY EVER PRESSED A QUARREL AGAINST READS AS THE RUNG BELOW, and
#     a plan that loses nothing reads as the line handed, all 16 pairs -- this
#     arc's standing generalization test, one tier further out.
#
# Five RED paths were proven on metal before this witness claimed GREEN. Skip the
# read-back and the run refuses `HeedMisrecorded`. Count one position twice and it
# refuses `HeedMiscounted` -- reaching that one on the wire takes disarming the
# honest fold first, since the fold catches it before the run can. Stand under a
# byte nobody pressed and it refuses `HeedUnpressed`. Publish a regard where
# nothing ever stood and it refuses `HeedEarly`, which takes disarming both counts
# first, since the subtraction overflows before the refusal can -- the arithmetic
# is doing its job. Disarm every guard at once -- the note never written, the
# read-back skipped, the wire fold's read, and the harness read -- and the
# selftest calls itself GREEN while `caravan/.heeds/plan.regard` holds only the
# provisioning's zero byte, so an operator would read a clean outcome over a live
# quarrel and the run would report it heeded. Seeing that once is what makes the
# reading back a check rather than decoration.
#
# Checks read the selftest output natively (`contains`), never a shell grep over
# interpolated output -- REDS %76 / %85, the apostrophe loom.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/caravan_heed_witness.rish

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "caravan/bin/heed"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p caravan/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build caravan/heed.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]

assert build.ok else "caravan heed build failed -- ${build.err}"

# The reader this witness runs is built here rather than borrowed (REDS %92).
let read_bin_build = run ["sh" "-c" "env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build caravan/read.rye -femit-bin=caravan/bin/read"]
assert read_bin_build.ok else "caravan read build failed -- ${read_bin_build.err}"

# The board declaration the rungs below opened, unchanged.
let published = run ["sh" "-c" "caravan/bin/read caravan/systems/serial_three_clients_board.bron 2>&1"]
assert published.ok else "the board declaration could not be read"
assert published.out contains "domains 4 -- channels 3 -- regions 11 -- grants 22" else "the board declaration changed shape"
assert published.out contains "verdict: whole" else "the board declaration did not read whole"

# A fresh start for the stores, the doorbells, this plan's notes, and the
# reader's own box. Every quarrel this witness reads at the end was seated by the
# lap itself, standing in for the run that heard the person who pressed it.
let clean = run ["sh" "-c" "rm -rf caravan/.regions caravan/.channels caravan/.heeds caravan/.readers"]
assert clean.ok else "the region stores, doorbells, notes, and reader boxes could not be cleared"

let test = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest 2>&1"]
assert test.ok else "caravan heed selftest exited non-zero"
assert test.out contains "GREEN" else "caravan heed selftest not GREEN"
assert test.out contains "a plan run under a quarrel it inherited says so" else "the heed finding did not close"

# The heeding and its three standing refusals, read straight, before any
# dependent runs. The fourth, `HeedMisrecorded`, is answered in the same fold,
# since whether a published regard quotes the position standing is a question
# those two bytes can settle between themselves.
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether it reads under the quarrel it inherited" else "the heeding fold was not weighed"
assert test.out contains "three refusals stand by name: early, unpressed, miscounted" else "the three heed refusals did not stand"
assert test.out contains "a plan reads as though nobody had ever objected to it" else "an unweighing plan did not read as one"
assert test.out contains "the plan's word stands under a quarrel it inherited" else "the regard did not read as one"

# The seam between a quarrel and a word about one, proven as its own fold.
assert test.out contains "a quarrel survives a provisioning and the word about it does not" else "the regard was never parted from the position it answers"

# The endurance below it, unchanged and still weighed.
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether a pressed quarrel outlives the run that heard it" else "the endurance below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a pressed quarrel survives a provisioning" else "the position was never proven past a provisioning"

# The appeal, the tidings, the standing, the term, the escort, the record, the
# hearing, the delivery, the amendment, the recantation, the bearing, and the
# mend below, unchanged.
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether it reads what its reader says back" else "the appeal below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether it writes back to the reader who objected" else "the tidings below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether its marks carry the standing of their objection" else "the standing below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes how long the objection beside its word may stand" else "the term below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether its word is read beside the reading against it" else "the escort below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether its record may hold a disagreement" else "the record below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether it hears what its reader answers" else "the hearing below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether its own corrections travel" else "the delivery below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether its own corrections are addressed" else "the amendment below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether its own judgments answer to a later run" else "the recantation below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan names what it expects of a phase, and what it would accept of a loss" else "the bearing below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a repair still refuses by name: unread, whole, overreaching" else "the mend below stopped being weighed"

# The generalization tests: a plan that loses nothing reads as the rung below,
# and a plan nobody ever pressed a quarrel against weighs nothing at all.
assert test.out contains "a plan that loses nothing reads as the line handed, all 16 pairs" else "an unlost plan did not read as the line handed"
assert test.out contains "a plan nobody ever pressed a quarrel against reads as the rung below" else "an unpressed plan did not read as the rung below"

# The heed lap: one plan run twice over a quarrel an earlier run carried here,
# once publishing the outcome as though nobody had objected and once publishing
# that same outcome under the position standing over it. Every number stands
# still -- the work, the dependents, the correction, the journey, the record, the
# escort, the asking, the mark, the telling, the reading back, the position
# carried past the run, the settlement -- and only what the run says about the
# quarrel it inherited moves.
assert test.out contains "phases: 6 bare, 6 under" else "the two plans ran different records"
assert test.out contains "dependents: 6 bare, 6 under" else "weighing a quarrel cost work it should not have"
assert test.out contains "phases absorbed into a standing dependent: 3 bare, 3 under" else "the two plans absorbed different phases"
assert test.out contains "abandoned reach, conferred and never served: 3 bare, 3 under" else "the two plans lost different work"
assert test.out contains "phases re-seated to carry what was lost: 3 bare, 3 under" else "the two plans repaired different work"
assert test.out contains "standing judgments taken back on this run's own evidence: 1 bare, 1 under" else "the recanting rung stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "readings corrected where they were read: 1 bare, 1 under" else "the amending rung stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "corrections carried to the place their reader was reached: 1 bare, 1 under" else "the couriering rung stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "disagreements written into the record: 1 bare, 1 under" else "the disputing rung stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "published words standing beside the reading against them: 1 bare, 1 under" else "the abiding rung stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "standing objections put back to the reader who raised them: 1 bare, 1 under" else "the lapsing rung stopped asking under both plans"
assert test.out contains "marks carrying the standing of the objection they quote: 1 bare, 1 under" else "the standing below stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "raisers told how their own quarrel came out: 1 bare, 1 under" else "the tidings below stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "readers whose reply to the answer was read back: 1 bare, 1 under" else "the appeal below stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "positions carried past the run that heard them: 0 bare, 0 under" else "a run whose reader accepted carried a position forward"
assert test.out contains "inherited positions weighed into the run's own word: 0 bare, 1 under" else "the heeding did not part the two plans"
assert test.out contains "inherited positions left exactly as the rung below leaves them: 1 bare, 0 under" else "the other half of the count did not close"
assert test.out contains "plans reported carried under a quarrel nobody weighed: 1 against 0" else "the two plans answered the same quarrel"
assert test.out contains "work still standing when the supervisor exits: 0 bare, 0 under" else "the two plans left different work standing"
assert test.out contains "the plan, as an operator finally reads it: carried out whole bare, carried out whole under" else "a quarrel decided what the work came to"
assert test.out contains "breaks a named turn: 0 bare, 0 under" else "the weighing run broke an order its author named"

# What an operator reads is what the wire carries, and what a reader writes is
# what their own box carries. Every note is read here, outside the run that wrote
# it, exactly as each would be read by the person it was written for.
let settled = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.heeds/plan.settled"]
assert settled.ok else "the plan published no settlement an operator could read"
assert settled.out contains "c" else "the wire did not carry the carried settlement the repair earned"

# The one note this rung adds, published beside that settlement and read in the
# same reach. Together the four notes below are the rung in miniature: the work
# was carried, a quarrel from an earlier run still stands, this run's own reader
# accepted, and the word an operator opens says which company it keeps.
let regard = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.heeds/plan.regard"]
assert regard.ok else "the plan published no regard an operator could read"
assert regard.out contains "u" else "a plan carried under a live quarrel read as a word standing alone"

let standing = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.heeds/plan.standing"]
assert standing.ok else "the plan carried no position the next run could open"
assert standing.out contains "p" else "a run that weighed a quarrel withdrew it in the same act"

let plea = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.heeds/plan.appeal"]
assert plea.ok else "the plan published no plea an operator could read"
assert plea.out contains "a" else "this run's own reader was published as one still pressing"

# The reader's own reply, in their own box, outside this plan's wire entirely.
let press = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.readers/desk.press"]
assert press.ok else "the reader replied nothing at all"
assert press.out contains "a" else "the record and the reader's own hand read differently"

# The mark itself, carrying both the reading its reader holds and the standing of
# that objection, exactly as the rungs below write it.
let beside = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.heeds/plan.beside"]
assert beside.ok else "a run withdrew the mark its reader earned"
assert beside.out contains "s" else "the mark did not name the reading its reader holds"

let quarrel = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.heeds/plan.dispute"]
assert quarrel.ok else "an open record kept no disagreement at all"
assert quarrel.out contains "cs" else "the record did not name the plan's reading and its reader's"

let correction = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.heeds/plan.amend"]
assert correction.ok else "the plan published no correction an operator could read"
assert correction.out contains "bc" else "the wire did not name the two readings the correction stands between"

let address = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.heeds/plan.at"]
assert address.ok else "the plan kept no address for the reader who took its word"
assert address.out contains "desk" else "the wire did not name the place its reader was reached"

let box = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.readers/desk.told"]
assert box.ok else "the reader's own box was never written to"
assert box.out contains "bc" else "the reader's box did not carry the correction in the words they read"

let hand = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.readers/desk.said"]
assert hand.ok else "the reader answered nothing at all"
assert hand.out contains "s" else "the reader's own hand did not name the reading they hold"

let outof = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.readers/desk.outof"]
assert outof.ok else "the raiser of the quarrel was never told how it came out"
assert outof.out contains "t" else "a word that never moved was reported to its raiser as one that did"

let recant_note = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.heeds/plan.recant"]
assert recant_note.ok else "the plan published no recantation an operator could read"
assert recant_note.out contains ".r...." else "the wire did not name the one judgment this run took back"

let lost_note = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.heeds/plan.lost"]
assert lost_note.ok else "the plan published no loss an operator could read"
assert lost_note.out contains ".x.x.x" else "the wire did not name the three phases the plan lost"

# The dependents measure the loss in their own hands, exactly as the rungs below
# left them, and the follower that once spoke for the judgment falls with it.
assert test.out contains "falls as its author declared, holding 1 conferred arcs it never served" else "a falling dependent did not fall holding its conferral"
assert test.out contains "client_b: read 3 arcs of its own, 0 inherited at its first breath, 1 conferred, 0 returned, 1 still reachable at home" else "the dependent a conferral was made to did not read it as its own"
assert test.out contains "client_c: bytes differed" else "the follower that once spoke for the judgment came home after all"

say "GREEN: Caravan heed witness passed."
